# Pairs with ListedInSink. Production before the fix of #5418, with ids
# content-addressed: a full capture of an unchanged tree republished an
# existing backup's id with nothing to stop it while a retention pass was
# deleting that backup. The pass had listed and doomed the id, removed its
# row, and then deleted the sink manifest the republish had just rewritten
# and registered, so the catalog listed a backup the sink no longer held.
# The mutation drops the wait on the pass's reservation: a republish is
# admitted while a pass still holds its id retiring.
MODULE: ListedInSinkUngatedRepublish
TARGET: ListedInSink
CLASS: Invariant
SUMMARY: a republish does not wait for the pass retiring its id
PERTURBS: Acquire

--- FIND
    /\ \A p \in Passes : cap[c].id \notin prDoomed[p]
    /\ \A d \in Caps : cap[d].id = cap[c].id => cap[d].ph \notin Held
--- REPLACE
    \* MUTATION: no wait on the pass's reservation.
    /\ \A d \in Caps : cap[d].id = cap[c].id => cap[d].ph \notin Held
--- END
